course: dictionary
lesson: 6697
title: Ocean and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ocean names the huge body of salt water that covers most of the Earth. Read the clues around it. In «Most of Earth's water is salty water in the oceans; only a small part is fresh.», the words salty and fresh tell you what kind of water an ocean holds.
explain: Ocean can also name one of five big named parts of the sea: the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic Oceans. In «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami killed about 230,000 people in 14 countries.», the capital letters and the word Indian show that it means one named ocean, not all the water on Earth.
explain: Ocean also means a very large amount, as in oceans of time. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: An ocean is a huge body of salt water.
fact: Oceans cover about 71% of Earth's surface.
fact: The five big named oceans are the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic.
fact: «In fact they all join into one world ocean.» This shows that the oceans are connected.
fact: Tides are caused mainly by the Moon, and whales, sharks and coral live in oceans.
exercise: «Most of Earth's water is salty water in the oceans; only a small part is fresh.» What kind of water is found in the oceans? | Fresh water | *Salty water | Frozen water | Hot water
exercise: «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami killed about 230,000 people in 14 countries.» Which word names one of the five big named oceans? | *Indian | Tsunami | Countries | People
exercise: Mia says, «We have oceans of time before the bus comes.» What does oceans mean here? | Water in the sea | Waves at the beach | A kind of fish | *A very large amount
test: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» Where does this activity happen? | In the desert | In the sky | On top of the mountains | *On the ocean floor
test: «Long before Europeans came, the Indian Ocean was a busy trade world linking East Africa, Arabia, Persia, India, South-East Asia and China.» What did the Indian Ocean link? | *East Africa, Arabia, Persia, India, South-East Asia and China | Sharks and whales | Only the Moon and the stars | Mountains and deserts
exam: Ben says the Pacific is a small lake in a park. Using what you know about oceans, what is the Pacific? | *One of the five big oceans, full of salt water | A small lake in a park | A river that runs into the sea | A kind of wave
